{
  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "The current best (config_026: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile, acc=0.7250) has been identified, and all remaining scvi_n200 multimodal-multiprofile variants involve known-negative changes (avgpool, concat, resnet50, singleprofile) unlikely to exceed it. The key remaining uncertainty is whether pca_n2000, the only untested RNA encoder in the optimal multimodal-multiprofile setting, could be competitive. config_029 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile) is a clean single-factor swap from config_026, directly testing whether the learned scvi representation is truly necessary or whether a linear PCA projection suffices. Given only 2 experiments remain, this is the highest-information experiment: if pca_n2000 is competitive (~0.70+), it reveals an alternative design axis for the final experiments; if it is substantially worse (as scgpt was at 0.52), it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and the current best is near-optimal, allowing the last two experiments to focus on fine-grained fusion/aggregation tweaks around the known optimum."
}

